---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import { uniPallet } from '../../data/products/uni-pallet';

import gen1 from '../../assets/product/unipallet/aa4c71cf6fd121cfe04e6f4f44658228fc24d3dc.png';
import gen2 from '../../assets/product/unipallet/b51c849a126306442c7c8125b31b939b6c012f92.png';
import gen3 from '../../assets/product/unipallet/3646f31f282e3bd4dc653ab0a340337a03b2361c.png';

const generationImages = await Promise.all(
  [gen1, gen2, gen3].map((img) => getImage({ src: img, width: 1100, format: 'webp', quality: 80 })),
);

const generations = [
  {
    tag: 'generation 1',
    alt: 'Generation 1 Uni-Pallet',
    image: generationImages[0],
  },
  {
    tag: 'generation 2',
    alt: 'Generation 2 Uni-Pallet',
    image: generationImages[1],
  },
  {
    tag: 'generation 3',
    alt: 'Generation 3 Uni-Pallet',
    image: generationImages[2],
  },
];
---

<ProductLayout product={uniPallet}>
  <section class="up-gen" slot="after-options" aria-labelledby="up-gen-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="up-gen__intro">
        <header>
          <p class="up-gen__eyebrow">Generations</p>
          <h2 class="up-gen__title" id="up-gen-title">Decades of Innovation, Built Into Every Uni-Pallet</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="up-gen__lead">
          <p>We Invent Solutions. And we do it knowing the work is never finished.</p>
          <p>
            For us, innovation isn’t a single breakthrough—it’s the result of steady, deliberate progress over time. It
            starts by observing how our products move through real environments: how they’re handled, where they’re
            pushed, and the evolving challenges our customers face every day.
          </p>
          <p>
            From there, we question, test, and refine—again and again—until each design performs in the conditions it’s
            built for. Every iteration is shaped by real-world use, direct feedback, and the shared experience of the
            people who build, use, and support our products.
          </p>
          <p>
            We don't separate innovation from daily work; we build it in—through curiosity, experimentation, and
            continuous refinement.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Uni-Pallet reflects that process. Across four generations of design, each version responds to real-world
            material handling demands—improving performance through what we’ve learned over time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="up-gen__grid">
        <article class="up-gen__card">
          <div class="up-gen__media">
            <img
              src={generations[0].image.src}
              alt={generations[0].alt}
              width={generations[0].image.attributes.width}
              height={generations[0].image.attributes.height}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <p class="up-gen__tag">{generations[0].tag}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="up-gen__body">
            <p>At 17 lbs., Gen 1 established the foundation for Uni-Pallet.</p>
            <p>
              It demonstrated that a lightweight pallet could deliver the structural strength and durability required
              for demanding distribution applications. From the start, steel reinforcement provided the necessary
              strength while letting us validate the lightweight concept.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="up-gen__card">
          <div class="up-gen__media">
            <img
              src={generations[1].image.src}
              alt={generations[1].alt}
              width={generations[1].image.attributes.width}
              height={generations[1].image.attributes.height}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <p class="up-gen__tag">{generations[1].tag}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="up-gen__body">
            <p>Gen 2 marked a fundamental shift in how Uni-Pallet achieved strength.</p>
            <p>
              We eliminated steel reinforcement and replaced it with an engineered plastic structure, building
              structural performance directly into the pallet.
            </p>
            <p class="up-gen__label">Key advancements included:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>A 45-degree corner design to better deflect impact and reduce corner damage under repeated handling</li>
              <li>A shock-absorbing perimeter that significantly reduced side splitting during fork truck handling</li>
              <li>Directional structural reinforcement concentrated in the 40" direction</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              This directional reinforcement came from field observation: pallets were predominantly handled along the
              short side. In response, the pallet was redesigned to place structural strength where it was most needed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="up-gen__card">
          <div class="up-gen__media">
            <img
              src={generations[2].image.src}
              alt={generations[2].alt}
              width={generations[2].image.attributes.width}
              height={generations[2].image.attributes.height}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <p class="up-gen__tag">{generations[2].tag}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="up-gen__body">
            <p>The pallet continued to evolve with the market.</p>
            <p>
              As multi-pallet handling became more common, it required use of the 48-inch direction, creating the need
              for consistent structural performance regardless of pallet orientation.
            </p>
            <p class="up-gen__label">Key advancements included:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>A raised diamond surface to improve load stability</li>
              <li>Structural reinforcement in both the 40" and 48" directions</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              This redesign ensured consistent load distribution and performance regardless of handling orientation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .up-gen {
    background: var(--c-sec-1);
    padding-bottom: 150px;
  }

  .up-gen__intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 809px) minmax(0, 789px);
    justify-content: space-between;
    column-gap: 80px;
  }

  .up-gen__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font: var(--w-bold) 14px / 14px var(--ff-s);
    letter-spacing: 1.54px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-sec-3);
  }

  .up-gen__title {
    margin: 15px 0 0;
    max-width: 472px;
    font: var(--w-light) 30px / 33px var(--ff-r);
    color: var(--c-black);
  }

  .up-gen__lead {
    max-width: 654px;
    font: var(--w-light) 16px / 22px var(--ff-r);
    color: var(--c-black);
  }

  .up-gen__lead p,
  .up-gen__body p,
  .up-gen__body ul {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .up-gen__lead p + p,
  .up-gen__body p + p,
  .up-gen__body p + ul,
  .up-gen__body ul + p {
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  .up-gen__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 21px;
    margin-top: 113px;
  }

  .up-gen__media {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 519 / 380;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #efece7;
  }

  .up-gen__media img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .up-gen__tag {
    position: absolute;
    left: 23px;
    bottom: 21px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 6px 18px;
    border-radius: 25px;
    background: var(--c-black);
    color: var(--c-white);
    font: var(--w-medium) 16px / normal var(--ff-r);
  }

  .up-gen__body {
    margin-top: 27px;
    font: var(--w-light) 16px / 22px var(--ff-r);
    color: var(--c-black);
  }

  .up-gen__label {
    font-weight: var(--w-medium);
  }

  .up-gen__body ul {
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  @media (max-width: 64rem) {
    .up-gen {
      padding-bottom: 80px;
    }

    .up-gen__intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: 28px;
      column-gap: 0;
    }

    .up-gen__title {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: 28px;
      line-height: 32px;
    }

    .up-gen__lead {
      max-width: none;
    }

    .up-gen__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 48px;
      margin-top: 56px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .up-gen__tag {
      left: 16px;
      bottom: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
